cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "sdts: a preregistered small-data benchmark for tabular synthesis"
abstract: >-
  A preregistered benchmark asking below what training-set size deep
  tabular generative models (CTGAN, TVAE, TabDDPM) stop beating trivial
  statistical baselines (independent marginals, Gaussian copula, SMOTE),
  and whether the ranking between them is stable in that regime. Eight
  public datasets on a size ladder from 200 to 20,000 training rows, four
  natively small clinical datasets at true size, a 20-trial tuning budget
  and five evaluation seeds per cell, for 2,220 committed result files.
type: software
